X-SOURCE:IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20260627T233000Z
DTEND:20260628T013000Z
LOCATION:Auer Hall &amp\; LIVE@jacobs
SUMMARY:Émile Naoumoff\, piano
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy this performance from almost anywhere in the world viaL
 IVE@jacobs!Repertoire  Beethoven: Sonata in F Minor\, Op. 2 No. 1: (1795)
 Chopin: Mazurka in F Minor\, Op. 68 No. 4 (1849)Chopin: Waltz in C-Sharp 
 Minor\, Op. 64 No. 2 (1847)Chopin: Nocturne in D-Flat Major\, Op. 27 No. 
 2 (1836)Chopin: Prelude in -Flat Major\, Op. 28 No. 15 (c.1839)Chopin: Et
 ude in E-Flat Minor\, Op. 10 No. 6 (1832)Rachmaninoff: Étude-tableau in 
 E-Flat Minor\, Op. 39: No. 5 (1917)Scriabin: Etude in C-Sharp Minor\, Op.
  2 No. 1 (1887)Brahms: Intermezzo in A Major\, Op. 118 No. 2 (1893)Naoumo
 ff: Romance in D Minor (2012)About the ArtistÉmileNaoumoff is professor 
 of music in piano at the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music\, wher
 e he has been on faculty since 1998. He has been likened to both Vladimir
  Horowitz and Arthur Rubinstein as a pianist\, displaying\, as one critic
  remarked\, the fire of the former and the poetry of the latter. He revea
 led himself as a musical prodigy at age five\, playing the piano and addi
 ng composition to his studies a year later. At age seven\, he became the 
 last disciple of Nadia Boulanger\, who referred to him as "the gift of my
  old age." At age 18\, he was signed by music publisher Schott\, Mainz. N
 aoumoff studied with Boulanger until her death\, permitting him also to w
 ork with Clifford Curzon\, Igor Markevitch\, and Robert and Gaby Casadesu
 s\, among others. Yehudi Menuhin conducted the premiere of Naoumoff's fir
 st piano concerto\, with him as soloist\, when Noumoff was 10 years old. 
 Naoumoff pursued studies at the Paris Conservatory with Lelia Gousseau\, 
 Pierre Sancan\, and Geneviève Joy\, as well as at the École Normale de 
 Musique de Paris with Pierre Dervaux (conducting). Upon Boulanger's death
 \, he assumed her classes at the summer sessions of the Conservatoire d'A
 rt Americain (Fontainebleau). He was later appointed to the Conservatoire
  National Supérieur de Musique\, Paris. Naoumoff is regularly invited to
  perform by the world's premier orchestras\, including the Los Angeles Ph
 ilharmonic\, Berlin Symphony\, and Vienna Symphony\, among many others. H
 e has worked closely with such conductors as Leonard Bernstein\, Leonard 
 Slatkin\, and Mstislav Rostropovich. He has also collaborated with a host
  of noteworthy musicians\, including Jean-Pierre Rampal\, Gerard Souzay\,
  and Yo-Yo Ma. Naoumoff has been invited to perform at numerous music fes
 tivals\, such as the Santander Summer Masterclasses\, Verbier Academy Fes
 tival\, Banff Center\, and residencies at the Conservatory of Barcelona. 
 He is an avid composer of French mélodies and is known for his transcrip
 tions for the piano. He maintains a video journal of daily improvisations
  on his YouTube channel. Meeting URL: https://liveatjacobs.music.indiana.
 edu/
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Enjoy this performance from almos
 t anywhere in the world via</strong><a href="https://liveatjacobs.music.i
 ndiana.edu/"><strong>LIVE@jacobs</strong></a><strong>!<br /></strong></p>
 <p><strong>Repertoire</strong><br />  Beethoven: <em>Sonata in F Minor\, 
 Op. 2 No. 1: (1795)<br /></em>Chopin: <em>Mazurka in F Minor\, Op. 68 No.
  4 (1849)<br /></em>Chopin: <em>Waltz in C-Sharp Minor\, Op. 64 No. 2 (18
 47)<br /></em>Chopin: <em>Nocturne in D-Flat Major\, Op. 27 No. 2 (1836)<
 br /></em>Chopin: <em>Prelude in -Flat Major\, Op. 28 No. 15 (c.1839)<br 
 /></em>Chopin: <em>Etude in E-Flat Minor\, Op. 10 No. 6 (1832)<br /></em>
 Rachmaninoff: <em>Étude-tableau in E-Flat Minor\, Op. 39: No. 5 (1917)<b
 r /></em>Scriabin: <em>Etude in C-Sharp Minor\, Op. 2 No. 1 (1887)<br /><
 /em>Brahms: <em>Intermezzo in A Major\, Op. 118 No. 2 (1893)<br /></em>Na
 oumoff: <em>Romance in D Minor (2012)<br /></em><br /><strong>About the A
 rtist</strong><br /><br /><strong>Émile</strong><strong>Naoumoff</strong
 > is professor of music in piano at the Indiana University Jacobs School 
 of Music\, where he has been on faculty since 1998. He has been likened t
 o both Vladimir Horowitz and Arthur Rubinstein as a pianist\, displaying\
 , as one critic remarked\, the fire of the former and the poetry of the l
 atter. He revealed himself as a musical prodigy at age five\, playing the
  piano and adding composition to his studies a year later. At age seven\,
  he became the last disciple of Nadia Boulanger\, who referred to him as 
 "the gift of my old age." At age 18\, he was signed by music publisher Sc
 hott\, Mainz. Naoumoff studied with Boulanger until her death\, permittin
 g him also to work with Clifford Curzon\, Igor Markevitch\, and Robert an
 d Gaby Casadesus\, among others. Yehudi Menuhin conducted the premiere of
  Naoumoff's first piano concerto\, with him as soloist\, when Noumoff was
  10 years old. Naoumoff pursued studies at the Paris Conservatory with Le
 lia Gousseau\, Pierre Sancan\, and Geneviève Joy\, as well as at the Éc
 ole Normale de Musique de Paris with Pierre Dervaux (conducting). Upon Bo
 ulanger's death\, he assumed her classes at the summer sessions of the Co
 nservatoire d'Art Americain (Fontainebleau). He was later appointed to th
 e Conservatoire National Supérieur de Musique\, Paris. Naoumoff is regul
 arly invited to perform by the world's premier orchestras\, including the
  Los Angeles Philharmonic\, Berlin Symphony\, and Vienna Symphony\, among
  many others. He has worked closely with such conductors as Leonard Berns
 tein\, Leonard Slatkin\, and Mstislav Rostropovich. He has also collabora
 ted with a host of noteworthy musicians\, including Jean-Pierre Rampal\, 
 Gerard Souzay\, and Yo-Yo Ma. Naoumoff has been invited to perform at num
 erous music festivals\, such as the Santander Summer Masterclasses\, Verb
 ier Academy Festival\, Banff Center\, and residencies at the Conservatory
  of Barcelona. He is an avid composer of French mélodies and is known fo
 r his transcriptions for the piano. He maintains a video journal of daily
  improvisations on his YouTube channel.</p> Meeting URL: https://liveatja
 cobs.music.indiana.edu/
