SUMMARY:Winston Choi\, piano
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy this performance from almost anywhere in the world viaL
 IVE@jacobs!Repertoire to be announcedAbout the Artist  Canadian pianist W
 inston Choi is professor and program director of piano at Roosevelt Unive
 rsity's Chicago College of Performing Arts. Winner of France's Concours I
 nternational de Piano 20e siècle d'Orléans and laureate of the Honens I
 nternational Piano Competition\, he is internationally recognized for his
  bold interpretations of the standard repertoire and his unwavering commi
 tment to contemporary music. He appears worldwide as a soloist\, chamber 
 musician\, and educator. Choi has performed concertos with numerous North
  American and international orchestras\, including the Civic Orchestra of
  Chicago\, Calgary Philharmonic\, Victoria Symphony\, l'Orchestre Nationa
 l de Lille\, and Colombia's national orchestra. His solo recitals have br
 ought him to such major venues as Carnegie-Weill Recital Hall\, the Kenne
 dy Center\, and France's Salle Cortot. A prolific chamber musician\, he t
 ours widely as a member of Civitas Ensemble\, Duo Diorama (with violinist
  MingHuan Xu)\, and Trio Diorama (with Xu and cellist Nick Photinos)\, an
 d recently performed with Matthias Goerne at the Ravinia Festival. A pass
 ionate advocate for new music\, Choi has premiered and commissioned over 
 100 works. His recordings include Elliott Carter's complete piano music\,
  Jacques Lenot's works (winner of the Grand Prix du Disque)\, and music b
 y Thomas Adès. He appears on such labels as BIS\, Cedille\, and Naxos\, 
 and is a core member of Ensemble Dal Niente. He earned degrees from India
 na and Northwestern Universities\, and studied with Menahem Pressler and 
 Ursula Oppens. A dedicated pedagogue\, Choi is also in demand as a master
  class clinician and conference presenter\, sharing insights on phrasing\
 , technique\, and interpretation. Meeting URL: https://liveatjacobs.music
 .indiana.edu/
